Description: native Wayland GLES3 screensavers for NCZ-OS
 A set of 74 OpenGL ES 3 screensavers that run directly on Wayland through
 wlr-layer-shell and EGL, with no X11 or Xwayland dependency: the Black Hole
 simulation (with stylized, kipthorne and faithful color modes), hyprsaver and
 Shadertoy-style shader hacks, the original Fractasia and Magmasimplex
 (molten-wax lava lamp) savers, and eleven ported classic hacks.
 .
 The hack binaries are installed in /usr/lib/ncz-screensavers, their shaders
 in /usr/share/ncz-screensavers/shaders, the chooser catalog in
 /usr/share/ncz-screensaver-chooser/hacks.tsv and the dev.ncz.screensaver
 GSettings schema in /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas.
 .
 The project is licensed under Apache-2.0 (see /usr/share/doc/ncz-screensavers/
 LICENSE and NOTICE): the grant covers the NCZ-authored harness, launcher,
 plugin, tools and in-house engines only. Each screensaver is a separate
 program, and the vendored and ported hacks keep their own licences and
 notices (MIT, CC0-1.0, CC-BY-3.0 and the xscreensaver permission notice); see
 /usr/share/doc/ncz-screensavers/copyright, NOTICES.md and PROVENANCE.tsv.
 .
 The settings UI on NCZ-OS is the Singularity plugin (ncz-screensavers-plugin,
 installed by the NCZ-OS image).
 Other distributions can drive the engine through the ncz-screensaver command
 line; ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference is a GTK4 reference front end.
 Version 0.7.0 moved the old standalone settings application out of this
 package.

Package: ncz-screensavers-gtk4-reference
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ncz-screensavers (>= ${source:Version}),
 python3,
 python3-gi,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
Suggests:
 gir1.2-adw-1,
Replaces: ncz-screensavers (<< 0.7.0)
Breaks: ncz-screensavers (<< 0.7.0)
Description: reference GTK4 front end for the ncz-screensavers engine
 A reference application for distributions and desktops that want to implement
 the ncz-screensavers engine on Wayland. It is a GTK4 settings window that uses
 only the public ncz-screensaver command line, the shipped catalogue and option
 files and the dev.ncz.screensaver GSettings schema; see docs/CLI-CONTRACT.md
 and docs/IMPLEMENTING-ON-ANOTHER-DISTRO.md in the source.
 .
 The window is built with libadwaita when it is installed and falls back to
 plain GTK4 widgets when it is not, so it also runs on desktops that ship GTK4
 without libadwaita; gir1.2-adw-1 is therefore only suggested.
 .
 It is released together with the engine and is not part of the NCZ-OS image:
 the NCZ-OS image hook refuses to install this package, and the settings UI on
 NCZ-OS is the Singularity plugin (ncz-screensavers-plugin) instead.
